  "raw_text": "{\n  \"options\": [\n    \"Widespread vaccination within a community confers protection to individuals who are unable to receive the vaccine, such as newborns.\",\n    \"The phenomenon known as herd immunity is achieved when sufficient individuals in a population are vaccinated, thereby safeguarding those who cannot be vaccinated, including infants.\",\n    \"In a population where a majority are immunized, unvaccinated members, particularly infants, benefit from the collective immunity.\",\n    \"The establishment of herd immunity occurs when a substantial proportion of the community is vaccinated, consequently shielding vulnerable individuals, including newborns, from vaccine-preventable diseases.\",\n    \"Herd immunity is attained when the vaccination rate is high enough to protect unvaccinated individuals, including newborns, within a community.\"\n  ]\n}",
