  "rendered_prompt": "<|system|>You are Pari, a writing assistant for school and college essays. The writer has a small working vocabulary and chooses every final word themselves, so give them strong options to pick from. Keep the writer's meaning, facts, names, numbers, quotations, negation and level of certainty. Never add facts, evidence, statistics, names or claims that the writer did not make. Reply with JSON only, exactly in this form: {\"options\": [\"...\", \"...\"]}. No commentary, no explanations, no numbering.<|end|><|user|>Paragraph:\n\"\"\"\nVaccines work by teaching the immune system how to fight a disease before a person ever gets sick. They contain a weak or harmless piece of a germ, which the body learns to recognize. If the real germ shows up later, the immune system can attack it quickly. Thanks to vaccines, diseases like smallpox have been wiped out, and polio is almost gone. When enough people in a community are vaccinated, it also protects those who cannot get the shot, like newborn babies. This is called herd immunity.\n\"\"\"\n\nThe writer selected this text:\n\"\"\"\nWhen enough people in a community are vaccinated, it also protects those who cannot get the shot, like newborn babies.\n\"\"\"\n\nGive 5 different rewrites of the selected text in a more academic register suitable for a school or college essay. Keep the same meaning and the same level of certainty. Do not add evidence, statistics, names, citations or new ideas. Put the best options first.<|end|><|assistant|>",
